{"abstract":"This document amends the U.S. Customs and Border Protection (CBP) regulations to implement an indefinite suspension of the de minimis administrative exemption for imports valued at $800 or less arriving through the international postal network. This document also establishes a new postal informal entry process for certain merchandise entering the United States through the mail environment.","action":"Interim final rule; request for comments.","agencies":[{"raw_name":"DEPARTMENT OF HOMELAND SECURITY","name":"Homeland Security Department","id":227,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/homeland-security-department","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/227","parent_id":null,"slug":"homeland-security-department"},{"raw_name":"U.S. Customs and Border Protection","name":"U.S. Customs and Border Protection","id":501,"url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/agencies/u-s-customs-and-border-protection","json_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/api/v1/agencies/501","parent_id":227,"slug":"u-s-customs-and-border-protection"}],"body_html_url":"https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/full_text/html/2026/06/24/2026-12669.html","cfr_references":[{"chapter":null,"citation_url":null,"part":"145","title":19}],"citation":"91 FR 37801","comment_url":null,"comments_close_on":"2026-07-24","correction_of":null,"corrections":[],"dates":"Effective date: This interim final rule is effective on July 24, 2026, except for amendatory instruction 4 (19 CFR 145.31), which is effective on June 24, 2026.","disposition_notes":null,"docket_ids":["USCBP-2026-0761","CBP Dec. 26-13"],"dockets":[{"supporting_documents":[],"agency_name":"USCBP","documents":[{"comment_count":11,"comment_start_date":"2026-06-24","updated_at":"2026-07-25T01:56:44.656-04:00","comment_url":"https://www.regulations.gov/commenton/USCBP-2026-0761-0001","allow_late_comments":false,"id":"USCBP-2026-0761-0001","comment_end_date":"2026-07-25","regulations_dot_gov_open_for_comment":false}],